{
  "version": "1.0.2",
  "notes": "Real hardware run of modem_power_cycle_test.py (1.0.1) found two bugs at once. (1) It used AT+CPOWD=1, which is WRONG for this module -- that's a SIMCom SIM800/900 series command; confirmed against this module's own official AT manual, the correct command for SIM7500/SIM7600 series is plain AT+CPOF. AT+CPOWD correctly returned ERROR on real hardware. (2) That exposed a real logic bug in the test itself: it never checked whether the power-down command actually returned OK before concluding anything about the wake sequence -- so it printed a false 'PASS' even though the modem never actually powered off at all (of course it still responded to AT afterward; it was never off). Fixed both: now sends AT+CPOF, and reports a distinct 'INCONCLUSIVE' result (instead of a false PASS) if the power-down command itself doesn't return OK, so a future run can't repeat this exact false-positive.",
